 is unchanged and approving on both sides, equals its copy at the commit, and has an accepted CLARITY amendment verdict binding its equal approved-text digest. An unreadable or unparseable live registry or copy yields a refusal naming it. The slot's loop-lane held-status rung does not run. Under the loop marker, a commit outside a claimed lane, other than a squash landing, is refused when it moves a held status or makes a held approval claim; a marked commit inside a lane is judged at landing. An unmarked plain trunk commit is not judged. A row tagged both MEANING and CLARITY reads MEANING, and a MEANING+BLESS ruling is no exception.\"\r\ntest_refs = \"TC-241; TC-278\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nphase = 6\r\n\r\n[design.LLR-247]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-209\"]\r\ntitle = \"The loop provenance trailer and the loop marker\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/provenance.py;project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py\"\r\ncode_symbol = \"LOOP_TRAILER/LOOP_SESSION_ENV/format_loop_trailer/parse_loop_trailer/loop_trailer_refusal/append_trailer\"\r\ndetail = \"kitlib/provenance.py, importing no sibling script, declares LOOP_TRAILER = \\\"Loop-Session\\\" and LOOP_SESSION_ENV = \\\"KIT_LOOP_SESSION\\\". format_loop_trailer(session) renders the trailer line; parse_loop_trailer(message) returns the last trailer's session or None; loop_trailer_refusal(message, session) names the commit subject when the trailer is missing, malformed, or names another session. dispatch.run and agent_loop.main outside interactive mode set the marker in their own process environment once per run, never in a launcher script, so child sessions inherit it and a person's shell does not.\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nphase = 6\r\n\r\n[design.LLR-248]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-209\"]\r\ntitle = \"Every loop writer carries the trailer, and the floor checks it\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;p